KZ3 patch 2160 (ENHANCEMENT, experimental): let ports register temporal backends through rsx_upscale.

Reserved backends such as FSR 3 and XeSS remain unimplemented by the generic toolkit until a port registers a
complete create/destroy/evaluate operation table. Built-in None and FSR 1 cannot be replaced. Runtime sharpness
changes reuse the active context, while backend changes are handled by the renderer integration in patch 2161.

Keep Scaling filter limited to Bilinear and Nearest. A separate, opt-in GUM flag adds Upscaler
(Off / FSR 3.1 experimental), FSR sharpness, confirmation, tooltip, initialization, and reset behavior. This keeps
the generic display page unchanged for ports that do not provide FSR 3.

Host coverage: tools/smoke/test_upscale.c and tools/smoke/test_display_mode.c.

